cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
title: "The class number of B_{23,1} is 1: an unconditional computer-assisted proof"
abstract: >-
  A certificate and an exact verifier proving, without assuming the
  Generalized Riemann Hypothesis, that the first layer B_{23,1} of the
  cyclotomic Z_23-extension of Q has class number 1. The proof combines
  Miller's explicit-formula bound on the class number with 99,222 totally
  split primes certified to have principal prime ideals, Masley's Rank
  Theorem and Iwasawa's theorem.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chakkour"
    given-names: "John"
    affiliation: "University of Toronto"
repository-code: "https://github.com/johnchakkour/b23-class-number"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - algebraic number theory
  - class number
  - cyclotomic Z_p-extension
  - Weber's class number problem
  - computer-assisted proof
